  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-06-23T00:48:30.338Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Problem: wanting to know which SDK is being used for compatibility reasons. and choose the sdk version accordingly and understanding which version one is on currently\nCurrently the SDK unity packages from the website give you the date, in the release notes we get the release name, date and build - so its relatively easy to correlate what version one is on. if they already are installed you still get your version.txt - this is great for understanding and navigating compatibility issues\nwith the Package manager for VCC you only get a running version number like 3.0.9, which seem to be not used anywhere else. \nproposed solutions:\n- in the release pages add this information to the pages. say \n'VRChat 2022.2.1p4\nRelease - 2 Jun 2022 - Build 1205 - 3.0.9'\n- have a version.txt in the package as well, (or add to package.json, not entirely sure where the best spot for it is)\n- have say the publish date included to be visible within the unity package manager, and and display this in VCC as well, similar to how \nthis would make it clear which version one has downloaded and installed by inspecting the package files or package manager or directly within VCC both at project creation and while maintaining it.",
